---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Cards from '../components/Cards.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
---

<Page path="docs">
<section id="shape">
  <h2 id="shape"><a href="#shape">The shape of it</a></h2>
  <p>One file says which repositories your system is made of and how to run them. A universe is one copy of all of it: each repository's compose files started as a compose project of their own, each with its own network. That is where the isolation comes from &mdash; two universes share no network, so nothing in one can reach the other's services.</p>
  <Figure>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 720 724" role="img" aria-labelledby="at ad">
      <title id="at">How a universe is composed: one manifest, two universes, a compose project and a private network per repository</title>
      <desc id="ad">A multiverse.yaml at the top names which repositories the system is made of and how to run them. Below it, two universes side by side: universe 1 on branch feat/login and universe 2 on branch main. Each holds the same two repositories, api and web, each started as its own compose project — acme-u1-api, acme-u1-web for the first, acme-u2-api, acme-u2-web for the second — and each project on its own network, named after it. A dashed wall between the two universes marks that they share no network. Below both, one shared reverse proxy gives every address of every universe a hostname.</desc>

      <rect class="d-box" x="210" y="20" width="300" height="98" rx="12"/>
      <text class="d-h" x="360" y="62" text-anchor="middle">multiverse.yaml</text>
      <text class="d-m" x="360" y="94" text-anchor="middle">which repositories, and how to run them</text>
      <path class="d-line" d="M360 118V152M185 152H535M185 152V188M535 152V188"/>

      <g>
        <rect class="d-box" x="20" y="188" width="330" height="378" rx="12"/>
        <text class="d-a" x="185" y="228" text-anchor="middle">universe 1</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="185" y="258" text-anchor="middle">feat/login</text>
        <path class="d-sep" d="M35 276H335"/>
        <rect class="d-tint-num" x="36" y="290" width="298" height="118" rx="8"/>
        <text class="d-t" x="185" y="320" text-anchor="middle">repo api</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="185" y="350" text-anchor="middle">compose acme-u1-api</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="185" y="380" text-anchor="middle">net acme-u1-api_default</text>
        <rect class="d-tint-num" x="36" y="424" width="298" height="118" rx="8"/>
        <text class="d-t" x="185" y="454" text-anchor="middle">repo web</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="185" y="484" text-anchor="middle">compose acme-u1-web</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="185" y="514" text-anchor="middle">net acme-u1-web_default</text>
      </g>
      <g>
        <rect class="d-box" x="370" y="188" width="330" height="378" rx="12"/>
        <text class="d-a" x="535" y="228" text-anchor="middle">universe 2</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="535" y="258" text-anchor="middle">main</text>
        <path class="d-sep" d="M385 276H685"/>
        <rect class="d-tint-num" x="386" y="290" width="298" height="118" rx="8"/>
        <text class="d-t" x="535" y="320" text-anchor="middle">repo api</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="535" y="350" text-anchor="middle">compose acme-u2-api</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="535" y="380" text-anchor="middle">net acme-u2-api_default</text>
        <rect class="d-tint-num" x="386" y="424" width="298" height="118" rx="8"/>
        <text class="d-t" x="535" y="454" text-anchor="middle">repo web</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="535" y="484" text-anchor="middle">compose acme-u2-web</text>
        <text class="d-m" x="535" y="514" text-anchor="middle">net acme-u2-web_default</text>
      </g>
      <path class="d-wall" d="M360 200V546"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="360" y="594" text-anchor="middle">no shared network</text>

      <path class="d-line" d="M185 562V618M535 562V618"/>
      <rect class="d-bar" x="20" y="618" width="680" height="86" rx="12"/>
      <text class="d-h" x="360" y="658" text-anchor="middle">one shared reverse proxy</text>
      <text class="d-m" x="360" y="688" text-anchor="middle">a hostname for every address of every universe</text>
    </svg>
  <Fragment slot="caption">One repository, one compose project, one network &mdash; per universe. The proxy is the only thing that reaches into all of them.</Fragment>
</Figure>
  <p>Nothing publishes a host port, because two copies of one stack cannot both have port 8000. One proxy holds one set of ports for the machine and tells universes apart by the hostname in the request, so the tenth universe costs no ports and changes no configuration anywhere. Your own compose files are not edited: the proxy labels, the dropped ports and each universe's own values go into a generated file beside your checkouts.</p>
</section>

